AUD_AMPLIFIER_HOST=host name or IP address of the Yamaha amplifier (optionally with :port)
AUD_AMPLIFIER_INPUTS="inputs to show with labels, e.g. AV5=Music App,HDMI1=Chromecast,TUNER" (optional, default all inputs of the amplifier; keep the quotes, devserver.sh sources this file)
AUD_AMPLIFIER_PLAYER_INPUT=the amplifier input the sound of the player arrives on, e.g. AV5 (optional, when set playing music turns the amplifier on and selects this input)
AUD_AMPLIFIER_CHROMECAST_INPUT=the amplifier input the Chromecast is connected to, e.g. HDMI1 (optional, when set casting turns the amplifier on and selects this input; leave unset when another environment already does this for the same devices)
AUD_CHROMECAST_HOST=host name or IP address of the Chromecast (optional, unset = the Chromecast is not watched)
AUD_TUNER_STATIONS_FILE=path of the tuner station list, a JSON file described in docs/aud/amplifier.md (optional, without it the tuner shows the presets stored in the amplifier)
AUD_MUSIC_ROOT=folder with the music, laid out as Artist/Album/tracks, described in docs/aud/library.md (optional, without it the music library is empty)
AUD_AUDIOBOOK_ROOT=folder with the audiobooks, laid out as Author/Book/Disc/parts, described in docs/aud/library.md (optional, without it the audiobook library is empty)
AUD_DATA_DIR=folder where aud keeps its data: the cache of the music scan, the queue, the playlists and the history (optional, without it every start scans all files and the rest is lost at a restart)
AUD_LOKI_URL=base URL of a Loki to send the log lines to, e.g. http://loki-host:3100 (optional, without it the log only goes to the standard output)
AUD_PLAYER=mpv, mplayer or fake (optional, default mpv; fake only counts the time of the tracks, for development without speakers)
AUD_MPV_COMMAND=the mpv program (optional, default mpv)
AUD_MPV_AUDIO_DEVICE=audio output of mpv, as listed by `mpv --audio-device=help`, e.g. alsa/plughw:0,0 (optional, mpv chooses)
AUD_SOLOIST_WS=WebSocket address of Soloist, e.g. ws://127.0.0.1:8765 (optional, without it Spotify is not used)
AUD_SOLOIST_HOUSE_WS=WebSocket address of the second Soloist, the house player that plays what the aud queue asks for, e.g. ws://127.0.0.1:8766 (needed with AUD_SOLOIST_WS)
AUD_SOLOIST_DIR=folder Soloist is installed in, for the health check (optional)
SOLOIST_API_KEY=API key of Soloist, used by dev-soloist.sh only (development)
AUD_SPOTIFY_CLIENT_ID=Client ID of a Spotify Web API app, for Spotify search (optional, use a separate app per environment)
AUD_SPOTIFY_CLIENT_SECRET=Client secret of that app (optional)
AUD_MPLAYER_COMMAND=the mplayer program (optional, default mplayer)
VID_MEDIA_ROOT=folder with the videos (optional, without it the video library is empty)
AUD_MPLAYER_AUDIO_OUTPUT=audio output of mplayer, the value of its -ao option, e.g. alsa:device=hw=0.0 (optional, mplayer chooses)

MEILI_MASTER_KEY=openssl rand -base64 32 (Meilisearch, dev compose; admin only, apps use a scoped key)
MEILI_URL=http://localhost:7700 (optional, without it search is disabled)

JWT_SECRET=openssl rand -base64 (length of secret )(eg. 128)
UXP_ENCRYPTION_KEY==openssl rand -base64 (length of secret )(eg. 128)

